Kura: continue the logical step when Musubi Tuner resumes from a saved state.

Upstream src/musubi_tuner/training/trainer_base.py (v0.3.5, commit
4e7c714, lines 2050-2054) starts every run with `global_step = 0` and a progress bar
from zero ("TODO skip until initial step"), also after `--resume` restored the model,
optimizer, scheduler, and RNG (`accelerator.load_state`, ~496, called at ~1896).
global_step names step checkpoints and states (~2242, ~2246), decides the save cadence
(`global_step % args.save_every_n_steps`, ~2232), and stops training
(`global_step >= args.max_train_steps`, ~2272). After a Resume this sets global_step to
the step the restored scheduler counted (its `last_epoch`, stepped once per optimizer
update on each process), starts the progress bar there out of max_train_steps, and runs
only the epochs the remaining steps need (`num_train_epochs`, ~1928, counted the whole
target; the loop breaks out of an epoch at max_train_steps but would start the next one
and train another step). Data order is unchanged: the epoch restarts from its beginning.
Kura's Musubi Tuner training-state contract (`native_progress: logical`) depends on this
patch.

diff --git a/src/musubi_tuner/training/trainer_base.py b/src/musubi_tuner/training/trainer_base.py
--- a/src/musubi_tuner/training/trainer_base.py
+++ b/src/musubi_tuner/training/trainer_base.py
@@ -2047,11 +2047,18 @@ class NetworkTrainer:
                 init_kwargs=init_kwargs,
             )
 
-        # TODO skip until initial step
-        progress_bar = tqdm(range(args.max_train_steps), smoothing=0, disable=not accelerator.is_local_main_process, desc="steps")
-
         epoch_to_start = 0
         global_step = 0
+        if args.resume:
+            # Kura: continue the logical step the resumed scheduler restored (it steps once per
+            # update on each process). The epoch and data order still restart from the beginning,
+            # so run only the epochs the remaining steps need: the loop below breaks out of an
+            # epoch at max_train_steps but would start the next one.
+            global_step = getattr(lr_scheduler, "scheduler", lr_scheduler).last_epoch // accelerator.num_processes
+            num_train_epochs = math.ceil(max(args.max_train_steps - global_step, 0) / num_update_steps_per_epoch)
+        progress_bar = tqdm(
+            range(args.max_train_steps), initial=global_step, smoothing=0, disable=not accelerator.is_local_main_process, desc="steps"
+        )
         noise_scheduler = FlowMatchDiscreteScheduler(shift=args.discrete_flow_shift, reverse=True, solver="euler")
 
         loss_recorder = train_utils.LossRecorder()
